// REJECTS: Unknown permission scheme 'PUBLIC'
//
// `permissionScheme : PUBLIC;` on a SnowflakeApp. The grammar takes a bare IDENTIFIER there,
// so any word parses; SnowflakeTreeWalker:113 then resolves it against the
// SnowflakePermissionScheme enum -- {DEFAULT, SEQUESTERED} -- and throws for anything else.
//
// The reason this is the field to pin, and not the field next to it: `accountType` on a
// Snowflake CONNECTION is also an identifier, also enum-shaped, and is NOT validated. Upstream's
// own roundtrip test feeds it the literal value `BadOption` and expects it to parse. So the
// two identifier-valued enum fields of the same vendor have opposite parse-time behaviour, and
// a rewrite that picks a single policy -- validate all, or validate none -- is wrong on one of
// them either way. Verified: `accountType: BadOption;` is ACCEPTED by this same runner.
//
// Note this is the SnowflakeApp half of the two grammar files that share the stem
// `SnowflakeLexerGrammar`; see ../fixtures/t2-snowflake.pure, which covers both halves.
###Snowflake
SnowflakeApp fixture::neg::BadPermissionScheme
{
   applicationName : 'MyApp';
   function : zxx(Integer[1]):String[1];
   ownership : Deployment { identifier: 'appOwner'};
   permissionScheme : PUBLIC;
}
